# [IMPL-TCP_CONNECT_DIAL] [ARCH-TCP_CONNECT_CHECKER] [REQ-TCP_CONNECT_CHECKER]

TCP dial attempt with deadline and pure error classification into probe status literals.

## CLASSIFY_ERROR

<!-- [IMPL-TCP_CONNECT_DIAL] [ARCH-TCP_CONNECT_CHECKER] [REQ-TCP_CONNECT_CHECKER]: maps dial errors to OK/REFUSED/TIMEOUT/ERROR status literals -->

Contract:
  INPUT: err may be nil or a dial/network error
  OUTPUT: status literal OK, REFUSED, TIMEOUT, or ERROR
  PRE: err is nil or a dial/network error
  POST: returns exactly one of OK, REFUSED, TIMEOUT, ERROR
  EFFECTS: pure; classifies error category without I/O
  MESSAGE_CONTRACT: N/A — no message/event delivery
  RETRY: N/A — classification only
  IDEMPOTENCY: N/A — pure function
  TERMINATION: total

procedure CLASSIFY_ERROR(): # [IMPL-TCP_CONNECT_DIAL] [ARCH-TCP_CONNECT_CHECKER] [REQ-TCP_CONNECT_CHECKER]
1. IF err IS nil THEN RETURN OK
2. IF err indicates deadline exceeded THEN RETURN TIMEOUT
3. IF err indicates connection refused THEN RETURN REFUSED
4. RETURN ERROR

## ATTEMPT_DIAL

<!-- [IMPL-TCP_CONNECT_DIAL] [ARCH-TCP_CONNECT_CHECKER] [REQ-TCP_CONNECT_CHECKER]: dials one target within ctx deadline and returns classified result with elapsed time -->

Contract:
  INPUT: addr valid host:port; ctx carries per-probe deadline; dialFn injectable for tests
  OUTPUT: Result with address, classified status, elapsed duration >= 0
  PRE: addr is valid host:port; ctx carries per-probe deadline; dialFn injectable for tests
  POST: Result contains address, classified status, elapsed duration >= 0
  EFFECTS: opens TCP via dialFn; closes connection immediately on success
  ASYNC_BOUNDARY: await
  TIMEOUT: ctx deadline expiry → TIMEOUT via CLASSIFY_ERROR
  CANCELLATION: ctx cancel → dial aborts; CLASSIFY_ERROR maps to TIMEOUT or ERROR
  MESSAGE_CONTRACT: N/A — no message/event delivery
  RETRY: N/A — single dial attempt
  IDEMPOTENCY: N/A — read-only probe side effect is one dial
  FAILURE_MODES: TIMEOUT, REFUSED, ERROR per CLASSIFY_ERROR
  TERMINATION: returns when dial completes or ctx expires

procedure ATTEMPT_DIAL(): # [IMPL-TCP_CONNECT_DIAL] [ARCH-TCP_CONNECT_CHECKER] [REQ-TCP_CONNECT_CHECKER]
1. start := clock now()
2. conn, err := dial via dialFn on transport tcp to addr using ctx
3. elapsed := clock since(start)
4. IF conn IS NOT nil THEN close conn
5. status := CLASSIFY_ERROR(err)
6. RETURN Result with address addr, status status, elapsed elapsed
